From: Matthew Feickert <matthew.feickert@cern.ch>
Subject: [PATCH] Link against pthread on Windows

The bundled Mbed TLS is configured with MBEDTLS_THREADING_PTHREAD, so
mbedtls/library/threading.c needs the pthread_mutex_* symbols from
winpthreads. Upstream does not list it in PKG_LIBS, as the CRAN Rtools
builds link without it, but the conda-forge MinGW-w64 toolchain needs it
requested explicitly.
---
--- a/src/Makevars.ucrt
+++ b/src/Makevars.ucrt
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 # PKG_CFLAGS carries $(C_VISIBILITY) to hide the bundled nng_*/mbedtls_* symbols.
 PKG_CPPFLAGS = -Inng/include -Imbedtls/include -DNNG_STATIC_LIB
 PKG_CFLAGS = $(C_VISIBILITY)
-PKG_LIBS = -lws2_32 -lmswsock -ladvapi32 -lbcrypt -liphlpapi
+PKG_LIBS = -lws2_32 -lmswsock -ladvapi32 -lbcrypt -liphlpapi -lpthread
 
 MBED = mbedtls/library
 NNG = nng/src
